<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">July Monarchy</h1><p class="st-meta">1830 CE – 1848 CE · capital Paris</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The liberal 'bourgeois monarchy' of Louis-Philippe, King of the French, which rose from the barricades of 1830 and fell to those of 1848.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The July Revolution of 1830 drove out Charles X of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bourbon-restoration">Bourbon Restoration</a>. Liberal deputies offered the throne to his cousin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-philippe-i">Louis-Philippe</a>, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orleans">Orléans</a>, who took the title King of the French and accepted a revised Charter that lowered property qualifications and limited royal power.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Government rested on a narrow electorate of wealthy men, and ministers such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francois-guizot">François Guizot</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adolphe-thiers">Adolphe Thiers</a> alternated in power. Railways, banking and industry grew, and the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a> continued. The regime crushed republican and workers' risings, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lyon">Lyon</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a> workers' revolts of 1831 and 1834. Guizot resisted all demands to widen the vote.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>An economic crisis and a banned campaign of political banquets led to revolution in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> in February 1848. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-philippe-i">Louis-Philippe</a> abdicated and fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-second-republic">French Second Republic</a> was proclaimed.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/july-monarchy.jpg" alt="July Monarchy" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Original: Unknown Vector: SKopp · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_France.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1830 CE – 1848 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Paris</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Louis-Philippe I, François Guizot, Adolphe Thiers</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of the French, Orléanist monarchy</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1839&amp;focus=july-monarchy" aria-label="July Monarchy on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4734 472 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where July Monarchy lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5054 728L5054 728M5054 728L5054 728M5054 728L5054 728"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5054 728h0M5054 728h0M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5054 728h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Paris. <a href="/atlas?year=1839&amp;focus=july-monarchy">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
